  "id": "no-labels",
  "after": "overview",
  "title": "No labels: the computer finds the groups.",
  "caption": "An imagined kirana shop. Each dot is one customer: how many times they visit in a month and how much they spend per visit. Nobody marked any customer, so there are no labels. Clustering still finds three groups (समूह, samooh). You then look inside each group and give it a name.",
  "alt": "Two panels with the same customer dots. Left: all dots grey, no labels. An arrow leads to the right panel, where the dots are coloured in three groups with dashed rings: monthly bulk buyers (few visits, high spend per visit), weekly family buyers (middle) and daily milk buyers (many visits, low spend per visit). Text: nobody gave the computer these groups; you look inside and name them yourself.",
